    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1029">

                <pb facs="0776" n="660" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg660"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312:52/254a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Consul General Hanna.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 27, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Department regrets profoundly your arrest by the Federal authorities and the
                    indignities to which you were subjected at their hands; and rejoices that you
                    escaped without physical injury. It sympathizes with you in the humiliation
                    which you feel at the outrage suffered by you as the representative of your
                    Government; question of redress will have due consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
